 and twenty people excited when  I didn't have a lot I wasn't ready I  wasn't ready I didn't have mechanics  level design worked out the the core  narrative still is in its infancy we  need to give Kratos a fresh start we  need to give the players a fresh start  we need to show him grow we need to  investigate a little bit more about what  it is to be in this world and look at  every decision we make through fresh  eyes the things we were looking at was  really trying to dissect what's  important what's important for the  franchise and then also from that list  what can we actually flip on its head  I think we have to be bold because if we  just release another game that is like  the previous games it's a very small  cross-section of people that are gonna  say that's exactly what I wanted for me  I think you just go back and play those  if you miss those because they're never  going anywhere I'm not gonna go back and  change any of those they're a great part  of our history but the sort of big  change the bold change takes constant  convincing constant years of just trust  me just trust me in previous games we'd  have an inch in and then we'd have core  mechanics and then we would build levels  from those core mechanics while working  out the sort of combat but we sort of  have our levels worked out with our  combat at the same time and this one  everything was getting started and  constructed and theorized at the same  time so across the board we were getting  an engine lighting the ability to build  a level right and a level itself well at  the same time getting all the mechanics  design well the same time figuring out  what the Corps combat loop is literally  everyone is waiting for another person  to finish something because they've got  something else like how can somebody  design a puzzle we don't know what the  puzzle mechanics are all right so we are  basically going over and over again  trying to figure out the solution to the  questions we haven't even figured out  how to ask yet because everybody's at  the same point like I don't ever want to  make a game like that again like that  that was the most that is literally the  most stress you could possibly deal with  it it's like designing a camera and a  film stock while shooting a movie  well then figuring out who you want to  be in it while writing it all in the  same day like everything being decided  and figured out on the same day across  the board it's it is not the way to make  speaking of risks I understand that  having a tray us as like a companion was  a challenge throughout development  that's a challenge is like the the  understatement of the year it was it was  the scariest thing like people were  freaked out about the no cut camera just  cuz the amount of work we had to do and  there are a few unknowns about it but  there's a lot that we could point to as  being okay I think we can figure this  out and there's nobody who's had the  failure story from it companions there's  a lot of failure stories from that right  and that's sometimes worse than having  no information it's just having things  that point to and say look how bad it  was here look how about it was here look  how about it was here and they're saying  if we're gonna take on the Campania  thing we're not going to do what anybody  else has done right the only reference  point I could give them was dead to  rights  I was like it's gonna be like the dog  right except we're gonna go even further  and that he is a a part of the narrative  he is a part of the growth of these  characters but he is also fully  integrated into everything he helps you  with puzzles he is an appendage in  combat so much show that I said think of  it like he's the magic and I feel like  we needed to look at it that he was just  as important to the gameplay loop as he  was to the narrative arc and they get  into that a little bit but then they'd  also realize that's massive and nobody's  really been able to achieve that and